{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Create or migrate local accounts mira, niko, and sana onto node2 while preserving each user's UID, primary and supplementary groups, account fields, home path, and login shell.","status":"indeterminate","summary":"The source identities and memberships are documented, but the attempted destination inspection never ran because the cluster lease had expired. No final node2 account state or successful migration action was captured.","evidence_ids":["source-account-identities","cmd-a597c1f0c1164e95","global:after_executor:node2:platform"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Preserve the users' password hashes and password-aging state on node2 so their existing passwords continue to authenticate.","status":"indeterminate","summary":"The source shadow records and legacy-password checks are direct baseline evidence, but there is no destination shadow comparison, aging output, or authentication test after migration.","evidence_ids":["source-shadow-records","source-password-authentication","cmd-a597c1f0c1164e95"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Copy the complete home directories to node2, preserving content and relevant metadata such as ownership, modes, directory structure, and symbolic links.","status":"indeterminate","summary":"Source file hashes, metadata, and Sana's symbolic link are fully documented, but no destination home-directory evidence was collected and no copy operation appears in the captured command timeline.","evidence_ids":["source-home-content","source-home-metadata","cmd-a597c1f0c1164e95","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Leave the original accounts and home directories on node1 unchanged.","status":"partially_satisfied","summary":"The prepared source state is directly documented, and every captured executor command targeting node1 was read-only and rejected after lease expiry. However, the final node1 state could not be observed, so unchanged accounts and homes cannot be conclusively verified.","evidence_ids":["source-account-identities","source-shadow-records","source-home-content","source-home-metadata","cmd-4c638a6457e84ab0","cmd-bae6dd1d213e48d2","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.2,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. cmd-4c638a6457e84ab0 and cmd-a597c1f0c1164e95 were read-only discovery commands, while cmd-bae6dd1d213e48d2 only attempted to read the boot identity; all were rejected because the cluster lease had expired. Thus none changed managed-system state. Final residue, service, exposure, and package-health checks were unavailable, which limits observation but does not establish an executor-caused hygiene defect.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4c638a6457e84ab0","cmd-a597c1f0c1164e95","cmd-bae6dd1d213e48d2","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The preparation evidence establishes the required source state, but the executor reached neither node after the cluster lease expired. There is no captured mutation or final destination evidence, so the migration, password continuity, and home-directory transfer remain indeterminate. Source preservation is supported by the absence of executable mutations but lacks a final-state observation.","limitations":["All three executor commands failed at the provider boundary with cluster_expired, so none produced live-system output.","Every after-executor lifecycle observation on both nodes was unavailable; consequently there is no final account, shadow, home, service, package, or residue state.","The provider-wide restart protocol was not completed on either node. Fixed after-prepare boot identities exist for node1 and node2, but there are no restart acknowledgements, different post-restart identities, or recovered service/data observations; cmd-bae6dd1d213e48d2 also failed before reading node1's boot identity.","The destination baseline hashes intentionally exclude the named users and groups, so they do not establish whether those destination accounts were initially absent or already compliant."]}
